Routes through the complete theory
The article proves the centered and coercive homogeneous global results, the local finite-partition
theorem and a genuinely nonradial planar application, alongside both independent local failure
constructions. This companion retains the full corrected record, including conclusions with incom-
parable hypotheses beyond the article’s selection. Shared matrix foundations are proved once in
Chapter 2.
Chapter 1 is the scope and implication map. Chapters 3 and 4 develop the comparison-energy
and inward-model mechanisms. For the global family questions, read the centered applications in
Chapters 4 and 6, followed by the noncompact homogeneous theory in Chapter 7. For moving
geometry, read the affine-critical preparation in Chapter 8 and the complete planar proof in
Chapter 9. Chapters 10 and 11 retain the distinct flat-contour and fixed-normal extensions; neither
is absorbed by the planar strict-contour argument. Chapter 5 tests the limits of the certificate itself.
Chapters 12 and 13 keep the two local negative regimes separate. Appendix A spells out the finite
rational certificate common to their seed construction. Chapter 14 and Appendix B distinguish
mathematical theorems, exact formal contracts, conditional results and execution evidence.
Original source snapshots, corrections and sealed audits are preserved. Appendix B records source
versions and complete theorem-level correspondence. Definitions, assumptions, questions and
historical execution records are distinguished from proved conclusions.

Attribution and research assistance. The literature record distinguishes known special cases,
standard tools, related results and unresolved priority. The Euclidean-norm result of Guo–Lewis and
the two-piece affine escape theorem of Xie–Wächter are prior work, not new discoveries here [10, 1].
