1.2.3 N3. Simple global counterexamples retained as corollaries
The deterministic seed gives failure on a coercive finite maximum of four affine functions, with a
unique minimizer. This retains global failure in the finite polyhedral and semialgebraic class. It is
not superseded by an accumulation-based local example.
Adding a common positive quadratic to the three-piece seed yields

