4.6.2 Polyhedral losses and penalties at nonzero solutions
Locally around any optimizer, a nonzero scalar affine residual has fixed sign and is smooth; a zero
residual becomes a centered absolute value or hinge. Hence smooth losses plus ℓ1 , fused/generalized
ℓ1 , finite hinge and quantile losses are covered locally under uniqueness. The minimizer is not
required to be zero. Finite polyhedral regularizers, and their piecewise linear-quadratic extensions
from Theorem 4.5.1, are also covered. Extended-valued constraints remain outside the finite-function
formulation.

