6.4 Residual penalties and affine-fiber lifting
For a scalar affine residual nonzero at the solution, its absolute-value or hinge term is locally affine.
A zero optimal residual produces a centered sublinear term. The same decomposition applies to an
affine-composed Euclidean norm: a nonzero optimal vector residual is locally smooth, and a zero
residual becomes a centered norm. Finite sums with a convex locally C 1,1 smooth part reduce to
Theorem 6.1. For a more general gauge, local C 1,1 smoothness at that particular nonzero residual
must be checked; a spectral penalty may fail it.
