γ(u, 0) = |1 + 2u|, vanishing only at the optimizer. Smooth points are affine critical only when
stationary. Thus (8.1) holds globally, but γ(0, t) → 0 while the objective gap tends to 1/4.
This is a geometric rank-loss example, not a BFGS counterexample. A sufficiently small neighbor-
hood of its actual optimizer excludes the rank-loss point.

