The affine-critical set also has finitely many actual semialgebraic path classes, where two points
are related when a continuous path with semialgebraic restricted graph joins them inside the set.
Each class is semialgebraic and internally connected by such paths. Every continuous semialgebraic
path admits the finite-exception regularity just specified on the same curve; for finite convex
semialgebraic F , its actual composition with F is likewise continuous and smooth off finitely
many interior parameters. The objective is constant on each class. Ordinary topological connected
components are separately finite and semialgebraic, with constant objective value; their identification
with path classes is not needed here.
