9.7 Local consequences and natural assumptions
Proof of Corollary 9.2. All cluster points have the limiting objective value. An affine-critical cluster
point is optimal by the extra hypothesis; hence that value is F∗ . Compactness gives distance to the
solution set tending to zero. Under uniqueness every convergent subsequence has the same limit,
proving whole-sequence convergence. For the local statement, compactness and uniqueness put
a sufficiently low sublevel inside any given neighborhood of x∗ ; Armijo then traps the accepted
iterates there.

