                          F (u, v) = ψ(u, v) + h(v),        u ∈ Rn−1 ,     v ∈ R,

where ψ is convex with locally Lipschitz gradient, h is finite convex and locally C 1,1 on R \ {0}, F
is strongly convex on the relevant neighborhood, and the minimizer has v∗ = 0. Here A = ∇u ψ,
irrespective of the singular normal derivative of h. The objective and the initial matrix may be
fully coupled.


