14.1 What the checks mean
Lean checks the formal proof term against its precise statement. Exact rational inequalities,
algebraic roots, actual matrix updates, objective derivatives, infinite sequences and geometric
existence arguments have different mathematical roles, but each retained assertion here has a
reviewed formal correspondence. An external numerical result is not imported as a proof. Compiler
logs are evidence of actual executions; they are not axioms and do not prove that an older execution
happened.
The principal results concern ordinary full BFGS. The negative seeds and their embeddings are
actual objective/run constructions. The positive framework derives its scalar hierarchy from actual
principal determinants. The stable-manifold conclusion in L follows from the actual return map
and a proved analytic argument, not a numerical starting vector assumed to lie on that manifold.
Exact formal hypotheses and dependencies appear in the complete claim index.

