whole theorem contracts and all dependencies, rather than offer a sample export as a substitute for
a proof.
The frozen corrected mathematical source is Git commit 00362c0249262d182866f14bac756a
7c4edac95c, with paths and hashes in editorial/BASELINE.json. The narrative revision
starts from the initial author-review release at 7f53b4c; its source manifest, original contract
reviews and unchanged earlier PDFs are preserved under editorial/narrative_rebuild/ and
release/history/20260912_initial/. All 172 corrected source spans remain present with their
complete exports. The new opening changes their scientific presentation and reading order, not
their mathematical assertions.
The revised article independently proves global centered and coercive homogeneous convergence,
local finite-partition and planar results, the actual-matrix framework and both finite-branch local
counterexamples. The noncompact homogeneous alternatives, fixed-normal geometry, flat-contour
parabolic family, lifting, rates and scalar baseline remain separate companion results. The infinite
constant-Hessian family in Chapter 13 also remains here after its removal from the article’s main
theorem selection. None of these incomparable results is treated as superseded merely because the
article selects a smaller statement set.

